-- title:
--   Genus of the q-expansion function field under algebraically closed constant extension
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ and $K$ be algebraically closed fields with $K$ a $\kappa$-algebra, and let $\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$. For a field $k$, [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC k \Gamma`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) denotes the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $k(\!(q)\!)$ over $k$ generated by all quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}_k(p_f)/\mathrm{intSeriesC}_k(p_g)$, where $f,g$ are modular forms of some weight $k_0$ for the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb R)$ admitting integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g\in\mathbb Z[[q]]$ and the coefficientwise image of $p_g$ in $k$ is nonzero. It is assumed that both $F_\kappa=$ `qExpFunctionFieldC κ Γ` over $\kappa$ and $F_K=$ `qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ` over $K$ are curves in the sense of `IsCurveOver`: all divisors of nonzero elements exist and have degree $0$, every place has residue field finite over the constant field, and the module of Kähler differentials is free of rank one over the function field. It is further assumed that each of $F_\kappa/\kappa$ and $F_K/K$ contains an element transcendental over the constants over which the whole field is finite-dimensional. The conclusion is the equality of genera $\mathrm{genusFF}(K,F_K)=\mathrm{genusFF}(\kappa,F_\kappa)$, where $\mathrm{genusFF}$ is the $K$-dimension of $H^1$ of the zero divisor.
--
--   This is the invariance of the genus of a function field of one variable under extension of an algebraically closed constant field, specialised to the $q$-expansion function fields attached to a subgroup $\Gamma\le\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$. It is used in the computation of the genus of the function fields of the modular curves $X_H$ at full level, where the constant field may be enlarged at will.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_genusFF_qExpFunctionFieldC_eq_genusFF_qExpFunctionFieldC_of_isAlgClosed.lean

